{"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"anchor":"Type-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Type Methods"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"symbolKind":"enum","title":"EntityCollapse","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}]},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"([E]) -> [E]"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"text":"The determinism requirement","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-determinism-requirement"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver must be a pure function of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assert"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}]},{"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A resolver’s output is read as "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}]},{"type":"text","text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"surviving"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ID are all updated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are lost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads and writes any "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"EntityDB","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"role":"symbol","title":"PersistableModel","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow for a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","role":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","title":"SwiduxPersistence","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" down to one, keeping the winner of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"E"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"preferring"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"E"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","role":"symbol","title":"byID(preferring:)"}}}